## Overview
#c1[overview,i5] Cobra structures CLI applications around commands, arguments, and local or persistent flags, executing command trees through root-directed execution flows.
  > README.md::Overview #311fca062beb
  > README.md::Concepts #61be5fc556df
  > README.md::Flags #ea2772b1c791
  > command.go:1090-1092 #981fcf1b6cb5
#c2[overview,i5] Execution traverses lifecycle hooks in order—PersistentPreRun, PreRun, Run, PostRun, and PersistentPostRun—and coordinates initialization and finalization callbacks across command invocations.
  > cobra.go::OnInitialize #05702d363add
  > cobra.go::OnFinalize #ca4ed14a041c
  > command.go:124-125 #fdec43d9aee0
  > command.go:117-122 #bb4c25112f98
  > command.go:974-982 #db72d026d21b
#c3[overview,i5] Cobra enforces argument validation via PositionalArgs functions like MinimumNArgs, MaximumNArgs, RangeArgs, and OnlyValidArgs, which can be composed sequentially using MatchAll.
  > args.go::PositionalArgs #fa0108b484b9
  > args.go::OnlyValidArgs #7e1a2b843717
  > args.go::MinimumNArgs #143de7231849
  > args.go::RangeArgs #bbb348206852
  > args.go::MatchAll #37ef1bb57361
#c4[overview,i5] Persistent flags inherit hierarchically through parent commands and merge into InheritedFlags, while flag groups enforce mutual exclusivity and co-requirement rules during parsing.
  > README.md::Flags #ea2772b1c791
  > command.go::InheritedFlags #8e35b5d2906b
  > command.go::updateParentsPflags #b85cd4633d19
  > flag_groups.go::const.MarkFlagsRequiredTogether #452856dc514c
  > flag_groups.go::validateRequiredFlagGroups.len #77cd43dcc964
#c5[overview,i5] Disabling flag parsing halts flag processing and bypasses flag group validation, required flag verification, and flag completion checks.
  > command.go::ValidateRequiredFlags #7915543e8adc
  > command.go::ParseFlags #04de7d6367a1
  > completions.go::completeRequireFlags #16f93dd08f2e
  > completions.go:658-662 #ff062a113020
  > flag_groups.go::ValidateFlagGroups #5246e195d668
#c6[overview,i5] Cobra automatically generates shell completion scripts for Bash, Zsh, Fish, and PowerShell by inspecting commands, arguments, and flag completion metadata.
  > README.md::Overview #311fca062beb
  > completions.go:785-787 #eae97131d05c
  > completions.go:929 #8a90e43f70bf
  > shell_completions.go:39 #3a0a61b69a62
  > shell_completions.go:68 #8234f2e7bb85
  > shell_completions.go:96-98 #b59420007f0f
#c7[overview,i5] Dynamic shell completion evaluates candidate completions alongside integer directives that control error handling, candidate filtering, and file completion behavior.
  > bash_completions.go:119-122 #875a2eb0782d
  > bash_completionsV2.go:87-93 #d9ab13f68e7a
  > bash_completionsV2.go:106-109 #b73fe8ca7683
  > completions.go::initCompleteCmd.func #7150b68c87c9
  > powershell_completions.go:206-213 #846f8602b8ca
  > zsh_completions.go:177-180 #fb7f546222c6
#c8[overview,i5] ActiveHelp displays contextual guidance marked by special prefixes in supported completion environments, while being suppressed by global or program-specific configurations and unsupported shells.
  > active_help.go::AppendActiveHelp #ca388bfb8121
  > active_help.go::GetActiveHelpConfig #971c4c5c059a
