  > powershell_completions.go:124-125 #78cffde7f271
  > zsh_completions.go:219-225 #059e8eb5dbb6

## (root)
#c9[i5] Cobra is a Go library for creating modern CLI applications with subcommand-based interfaces similar to git and go tools.
  > README.md::Overview #311fca062beb
#c10[i4] Cobra applications are built around commands, arguments, and flags, following patterns like `APPNAME COMMAND ARG --FLAG`.
  > README.md::Concepts #61be5fc556df
#c11[i3] Cobra automatically generates shell autocomplete for bash, zsh, fish, and powershell.
  > README.md::Overview #311fca062beb
#c12[i3] Cobra supports persistent flags that cascade through to children commands, as well as flags local to a specific command.
  > README.md::Flags #ea2772b1c791
#c13[i3] The Cobra library is installed by executing `go get -u github.com/spf13/cobra@latest`.
  > README.md::Installing #5bc0042d4cc1
#c14[i3] The `cobra-cli` generator tool is installed via `go install github.com/spf13/cobra-cli@latest` to bootstrap application scaffolding.
  > README.md::Usage #5b66dfef7bbf
#c15[i2] Cobra is licensed under the Apache 2.0 license.
  > README.md::License #5f620bbcdf49
#c16[i4] AppendActiveHelp prefixes activeHelpStr with activeHelpMarker ('_activeHelp_ ') and appends it to compArray.
  > active_help.go::AppendActiveHelp #ca388bfb8121
#c17[i3] The activeHelpGlobalDisable constant is set to "0", and activeHelpEnvVarSuffix is "ACTIVE_HELP".
  > active_help.go:26-29 #5583a0359ea0
#c18[i5] GetActiveHelpConfig returns "0" if the global environment variable is set to activeHelpGlobalDisable ("0").
  > active_help.go::GetActiveHelpConfig #971c4c5c059a
#c19[i4] When the global active help environment variable is not disabled ("0"), GetActiveHelpConfig falls back to the program-specific environment variable for the root command name.
  > active_help.go::GetActiveHelpConfig #971c4c5c059a
#c20[i3] activeHelpEnvVar formats a program-specific environment variable using configEnvVar with the command name and activeHelpEnvVarSuffix.
  > active_help.go::activeHelpEnvVar #077759b047b0
#c21[i5] PositionalArgs is a function type accepting a pointer to Command and a slice of string arguments, returning an error.
  > args.go::PositionalArgs #fa0108b484b9
#c22[i4] OnlyValidArgs strips descriptions following tab characters from cmd.ValidArgs and returns an error if any arg is not present in the sanitized slice.
  > args.go::OnlyValidArgs #7e1a2b843717
#c23[i4] MinimumNArgs and MaximumNArgs return PositionalArgs validators that enforce lower and upper bounds, respectively, on argument slice length.
  > args.go::MinimumNArgs #143de7231849
#c24[i4] RangeArgs returns a PositionalArgs validator that returns an error if len(args) is strictly less than min or greater than max.
  > args.go::RangeArgs #bbb348206852
#c25[i5] MatchAll combines multiple PositionalArgs functions and returns the first error encountered during sequential execution.
  > args.go::MatchAll #37ef1bb57361
#c26[i2] ExactValidArgs is a deprecated validator that delegates directly to MatchAll(ExactArgs(n), OnlyValidArgs).
  > args.go::ExactValidArgs #7ee6cfe98363
#c27[i3] Cobra defines Bash completion annotation constants for filename extensions, custom handlers, single required flags, and directory subdirectories.
  > bash_completions.go:29-34 #df6278a11299
#c28[i2] The generated Bash helper __<name>_debug writes log lines to the file path specified in BASH_COMP_DEBUG_FILE when defined.
  > bash_completions.go:41-43 #546532a528bb
#c29[i4] __<name>_handle_go_custom_completion invokes the target program using eval while disabling ActiveHelp for bash completion v1.
  > bash_completions.go:90-91 #346c91a8e775
#c30[i3] If a custom Go completion returns ShellCompDirectiveError, the bash handler aborts completion without adding replies.
  > bash_completions.go:119-122 #875a2eb0782d
#c31[i3] In Bash, setting a flag in local_nonpersistent_flags empties the available commands list so subcommands are hidden.
  > bash_completions.go:308-311 #385803101124
#c32[i2] Associative flag value tracking in flaghash is skipped for Bash versions equal to or earlier than version 3.
  > bash_completions.go:313-315 #373b4cdb395b
#c33[i3] writeCommands skips subcommands that are not available unless the command is cmd.helpCommand.
  > bash_completions.go::writeCommands.WriteStringAndCheck #b06e18370d6c
#c34[i4] prepareCustomAnnotationsForFlags acquires flagCompletionMutex and points BashCompCustom annotations for registered flags to __<root>_handle_go_custom_completion.
  > bash_completions.go::prepareCustomAnnotationsForFlags #d72f38e92919
#c35[i3] writeRequiredFlag emits flags annotated with BashCompOneRequiredFlag into must_have_one_flag, appending '=' for non-boolean flags and adding shorthand versions if present.
  > bash_completions.go::writeRequiredFlag #0043b32323c8
#c36[i3] writeRequiredNouns strips tab-delimited descriptions from cmd.ValidArgs and marks has_completion_function=1 if cmd.ValidArgsFunction is not nil.
  > bash_completions.go::writeRequiredNouns #ae366f107262
#c37[i3] writeCmdAliases guards alias array and hash definitions with a Bash version check requiring BASH_VERSION unset or BASH_VERSINFO[0] greater than 3.
  > bash_completions.go::writeCmdAliases.WriteStringAndCheck #a2541d68bb3a
#c38[i4] gen recurses through available child commands or helpCommand, generating completion functions named with spaces replaced by underscores and colons by double underscores.
  > bash_completions.go::gen.gen #751a7845cc5c
#c39[i3] The completion function name uses the suffix _root_command for the root Command, whereas other commands use standard _<commandName>().
  > bash_completions.go::gen #a55ed2a05cfb
#c40[i4] nonCompletableFlag considers a flag non-completable if it is marked as Hidden or has a non-empty Deprecated string.
  > bash_completions.go::nonCompletableFlag #423994695545
#c41[i4] GenBashCompletionV2 writes Bash completion version 2 script content directly to the provided io.Writer.
  > bash_completionsV2.go::GenBashCompletionV2 #483932c189df
#c42[i3] The generated Bash script selects ShellCompRequestCmd when includeDesc is true, and ShellCompNoDescRequestCmd when false.
  > bash_completionsV2.go:32-35 #7fb8690f7040
#c43[i3] The Bash completion script extracts an integer directive after the last colon in the program output, defaulting to 0 if absent.
  > bash_completionsV2.go:87-93 #d9ab13f68e7a
#c44[i3] When the error directive bit is set in the directive, processing immediately returns without providing completions.
  > bash_completionsV2.go:106-109 #b73fe8ca7683
#c45[i4] ActiveHelp lines are identified by matching activeHelpMarker prefix and parsed separately from regular completion candidates.
  > bash_completionsV2.go:257-266 #544038599a20
