  > bash_completionsV2.go:358-361 #8fcf4b17aa1e
#c47[i2] The keep-order directive (compopt -o nosort) requires Bash version 4.4 or higher.
  > bash_completionsV2.go:121-127 #e72f172e7e40
#c48[i3] EnablePrefixMatching defaults to false, controlling whether automatic prefix matching is enabled in CLI tools.
  > cobra.go::EnablePrefixMatching #593894bc8e9e
#c49[i3] EnableTraverseRunHooks defaults to false, meaning only the first discovered run hook executes unless set to true to traverse all parents.
  > cobra.go::EnableTraverseRunHooks #04602cf9ef35
#c50[i2] MousetrapHelpText defines a Windows splash screen when started from explorer.exe, and MousetrapDisplayDuration defaults to 5 seconds.
  > cobra.go::MousetrapDisplayDuration #01399a8aa2c2
#c51[i4] OnInitialize appends functions to run when each command's Execute method is called.
  > cobra.go::OnInitialize #05702d363add
#c52[i4] OnFinalize registers callback functions that are executed when each command's Execute method terminates.
  > cobra.go::OnFinalize #ca4ed14a041c
#c53[i3] Eq only supports comparing int and string kinds, and panics if called with array, chan, map, or slice types.
  > cobra.go::Eq #337155dc8fde
#c54[i4] CheckErr prints non-nil messages prefixed with 'Error:' to stderr and immediately terminates the process with exit code 1.
  > cobra.go::CheckErr #c610b83d1ca2
#c55[i3] WriteStringAndCheck writes a string into an io.StringWriter and delegates error handling directly to CheckErr.
  > cobra.go::WriteStringAndCheck #247570f8e9b1
#c56[i3] Cobra commands allow defining either a static ValidArgs completion list or a dynamic ValidArgsFunction, but not both on a single command.
  > command.go:89 #fec78efc93a6
#c57[i4] The *PreRun and *PostRun lifecycle hooks run only when the command's Run function has been declared.
  > command.go:124-125 #fdec43d9aee0
#c58[i4] Lifecycle run functions execute strictly in order: PersistentPreRun, PreRun, Run, PostRun, then PersistentPostRun, with child commands inheriting persistent variants.
  > command.go:117-122 #bb4c25112f98
#c59[i3] Executing a command with Execute or ExecuteC replaces a nil command context with context.Background.
  > command.go:266-268 #ab6a4e8e3999
#c60[i3] Default I/O streams fall back up the command parent hierarchy until reaching defaults: stdout defaults to os.Stdout, while stderr defaults to os.Stderr.
  > command.go::getOut #95340933a26b
#c61[i3] Default command usage is printed to OutOrStderr, whereas default command help is written to OutOrStdout.
  > command.go::UsageFunc #baba10552b92
#c62[i3] Setting a non-empty Version on a command automatically injects a boolean version flag and a shorthand v flag if they are not already defined.
  > command.go:111-114 #fda5f1b5e552
#c63[i3] Command templates and error prefixes inherit values recursively from parent commands if not explicitly set on the command.
  > command.go::UsageTemplate #4e94d393f815
#c64[i3] stripFlags strips recognized flag arguments and values from an argument slice, stopping immediately when reaching the '--' terminator.
  > command.go:688-690 #47f69e4b9865
#c65[i4] Calling ExecuteC on a child command redirects execution to its root command.
  > command.go:1090-1092 #981fcf1b6cb5
#c66[i4] When TraverseChildren is set, ExecuteC discovers commands via Traverse instead of Find.
  > command.go:1120-1124 #b4fb2c852c8d
#c67[i5] If execute returns flag.ErrHelp, ExecuteC invokes HelpFunc and returns a nil error.
  > command.go:1152-1155 #701a0bd58f7c
#c68[i4] If EnableTraverseRunHooks is enabled, persistent pre-run hooks run from root down to command, while persistent post-runs run up to root.
